msgid ""
msgstr ""
"# Layer Normalization Example\n"
"\n"
"This document demonstrates how to use the Layer Normalization layer in the network.\n"
"\n"
"## Overview\n"
"\n"
"Layer Normalization is a technique used to stabilize and accelerate the training of deep neural networks. Unlike Batch Normalization, which normalizes across the batch dimension, Layer Normalization normalizes across the feature dimension for each individual sample. This makes it particularly useful for recurrent neural networks (RNNs) and transformer models, where batch sizes may be small or variable.\n"
"\n"
"## Implementation\n"
"\n"
"The following code snippet shows how to add a Layer Normalization layer to your model:\n"
"\n"
"```python\n"
"import torch\n"
"import torch.nn as nn\n"
"\n"
"# Define a simple model with Layer Normalization\n"
"class SimpleModel(nn.Module):\n"
"    def __init__(self, input_dim, hidden_dim, output_dim):\n"
"        super(SimpleModel, self).__init__()\n"
"        self.fc1 = nn.Linear(input_dim, hidden_dim)\n"
"        self.ln = nn.LayerNorm(hidden_dim)  # Layer Normalization layer\n"
"        self.fc2 = nn.Linear(hidden_dim, output_dim)\n"
"\n"
"    def forward(self, x):\n"
"        x = self.fc1(x)\n"
"        x = self.ln(x)  # Apply Layer Normalization\n"
"        x = torch.relu(x)\n"
"        x = self.fc2(x)\n"
"        return x\n"
"\n"
"# Create an instance of the model\n"
"model = SimpleModel(input_dim=10, hidden_dim=20, output_dim=5)\n"
"print(model)\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Key Parameters\n"
"\n"
"- `normalized_shape`: The shape of the features to be normalized. This can be an integer (for 1D features) or a tuple (for multi-dimensional features).\n"
"- `eps`: A small value added to the denominator for numerical stability. Default is `1e-5`.\n"
"- `elementwise_affine`: A boolean flag indicating whether to apply learnable affine transformation (scale and shift). Default is `True`.\n"
"\n"
"## Example Usage\n"
"\n"
"Here is a complete example that demonstrates the forward pass of the model with Layer Normalization:\n"
"\n"
"```python\n"
"# Generate random input data\n"
"input_data = torch.randn(32, 10)  # Batch size of 32, input dimension of 10\n"
"\n"
"# Forward pass\n"
"output = model(input_data)\n"
"print(f\"Output shape: {output.shape}\")\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Advantages\n"
"\n"
"- **Stability**: Helps in stabilizing the training process by reducing internal covariate shift.\n"
"- **Independence from Batch Size**: Works well with small or variable batch sizes.\n"
"- **Suitability for Sequence Models**: Particularly effective for RNNs and transformers.\n"
"\n"
"## Conclusion\n"
"\n"
"Layer Normalization is a powerful and flexible normalization technique that is widely used in modern deep learning architectures. By normalizing across the feature dimension, it provides stability and improves convergence, making it an essential tool for training complex models.\n"

